From 8a6e99edeb08b1fa93ab82338723e13080e20b34 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Joan Torres Lopez <joantolo@redhat.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Feb 2026 12:21:54 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 47/54] gdm: Add fingerprint ready state to delay showing icon

Fingerprint mechanism now has a ready state that controls when it
appears in the authentication UI. When fingerprint authentication
starts, the mechanism is marked as not ready and filtered from the
enabledMechanisms list. Only after the fingerprint service has been
running for a brief window (0.5s) is it marked as ready and emitted
via mechanisms-changed.

This prevents the fingerprint icon from briefly appearing in the UI
for users who don't have enrolled fingerprints. In those cases, the
fingerprint service starts but quickly stops with service-unavailable,
so the timeout never completes and the icon never shows.
